# Which physical screen is which, pinned by what the monitor says it is.
#
# Installed to ~/.config/kanshi/config for the desktop user. kanshi is already
# running on this station - /etc/xdg/labwc/autostart starts it - and until now
# this file was zero bytes, which means the arrangement was whatever wlroots
# felt like on that boot.
#
# That is not hypothetical. Two probes of this Pi a few weeks apart found:
#
#   probe 1:  HDMI-A-1 (Philips) at 0,0      HDMI-A-2 (Samsung) at 1360,0
#   probe 2:  HDMI-A-2 (Samsung) at 0,0      HDMI-A-1 (Philips) at 3840,0
#
# Nobody moved a cable. With the layout free to flip, an absolute window
# position computed at boot is right until the next boot. Hence this file.
#
# The kiosk script does not depend on it - it asks wlr-randr for the current
# geometry every time it starts - but a pinned layout is what makes "the left
# screen shows the racks" a fact rather than a coincidence.
#
# Match criteria are "make model serial" exactly as the monitor reports them.
# wlr-randr prints that string in quotes, with a "(HDMI-A-N)" suffix added by
# wlr-randr itself - do not include that suffix here.
#
# Modes are given without a refresh rate on purpose. kanshi refuses a whole
# profile if any one clause cannot be satisfied, and a rate that drifts by a
# hundredth of a Hz between EDID reads would take both screens down with it.
# Without a rate, the highest available for that resolution is used: 59.8 Hz
# on the Philips, 30 Hz on the Samsung, which is what they run at today.
#
# Both screens are pinned at compositor scale 1 deliberately. Compositor
# scaling would change the pixel geometry the kiosk script reads back and
# then computes window positions from; the 4K screen is made legible by
# KIOSK_KISTEN_SCALE=2 instead, which is Chromium's own device scale factor
# and leaves the window geometry alone.

profile werkstatt {
	output "Philips Consumer Electronics Company PHILIPS FTV 0x01010101" enable mode 1360x768 position 0,0 scale 1
	output "Samsung Electric Company U28E590 HTPJC16451" enable mode 3840x2160 position 1360,0 scale 1
}

# A profile applies only when the connected set matches it exactly. Without
# the two below, unplugging either screen leaves kanshi with no applicable
# profile and the survivor gets the wlroots default - which is usually fine
# and occasionally is 640x480. Spell it out instead.

profile nur-regal {
	output "Philips Consumer Electronics Company PHILIPS FTV 0x01010101" enable mode 1360x768 position 0,0 scale 1
}

profile nur-kisten {
	output "Samsung Electric Company U28E590 HTPJC16451" enable mode 3840x2160 position 0,0 scale 1
}
